# Repository

- Contract lives in Domain: entities + `Result<T>` only. No Dio, DTO, Isar, or Flutter.
- Implementation lives in Data: coordinates remote/local sources, maps DTO → Entity, returns `Result<T>`.
- Repository is the single source of truth. UI and the presentation controller never read a cache or API beside it.
- Optimistic create/update: persist local → update UI → remote → roll back to the **exact** prior state on failure (not "refresh from server").
- Offline write queues (when in scope) persist in Isar inside the repository, survive process death, and resolve conflicts in the repository — never in the presentation controller.

```dart
// BAD — contract leaks DTO
abstract class CoursesRepository {
  Future<CourseDto> get(String id);
}

// GOOD
abstract class CoursesRepository {
  Future<Result<CourseEntity>> getById(String id);
}
```

UseCase: one operation, `call(...)`, returns `Result<T>`, depends only on the repository contract. No Flutter.
